{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Were it not that the enemy's wrath is gathered.</b> Were it not that the enemy's wrath is gathered against them to destroy — and if he could overcome them and destroy them, he would attribute the greatness to himself and to his gods and would not attribute the greatness to Me. And this is what is said: <b>lest their adversaries misinterpret</b> — they would 'misinterpret' the matter, to attribute their might to a foreigner whose greatness is not His — <b>lest they say, Our hand is exalted, etc.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:20.901505712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}